ith $dX^2 + dY^2 - dZ^2$.","caption":["The surface of $r$ and $z$ at one $t$ and one $\\phi$, a hyperbolic plane of curvature $-1/\\ell^2$, with the strip $0 \\le z < 2\\pi\\ell$ rolled up so that $z$ runs once round the axis: in flat space from $r = 0$ up and in three dimensional Minkowski space ($dX^2 + dY^2 - dZ^2$) below it, every distance along the surface the metric distance.","On it the metric is $dr^2 + e^{-2r/\\ell}dz^2$, so the lines of constant $r$ are horocycles, drawn as circles of radius $\\ell e^{-r/\\ell}$. Above $r = 0$ the strip is half of Eugenio Beltrami's pseudosphere, a horn that narrows without end. Below $r = 0$ the circles grow faster than the distance along the surface, and the strip opens toward a light cone of Minkowski space. Over every point of this plane stands a flat plane of $t$ and $\\phi$, its light cones turned through $\\sqrt{3}\\,r/2\\ell$."]}]}
